<refnamediv>
  <refname><function>SilikoValueCreate</function></refname>
  <refpurpose>Function to make a zero value</refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Value.h&gt;</programlisting>
<programlisting language="C">SilikoValue *SilikoValueCreate(void);</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <function>SilikoValueCreate</function> function creates a new
value. Its status will be <literal>SilikoValueInteger</literal> and
its integer value will be <literal>0</literal>.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Return Values</title>

<para><function>SilikoValueCreate</function> returns a
pointer to the newly created <type>SilikoValue</type> object if
successful, or <literal>NULL</literal> on failure.</para>
</refsection>
